# OJ Packaging

Build clean final packages in dedicated staging directories using an allowlist. Do not zip the whole workspace. Exclude logs, reports, candidate pools, provenance, caches and temporary files unless explicitly required.

The packaging pipeline must produce TWO final ZIP archives on success:
1. **Polygon Full Package ZIP**: for FuraOJ / VNOJ / Polygon.
2. **Themis Package ZIP**: for Themis automated grading software.


## Golden FuraOJ / VNOJ template

Use the user-provided Polygon package as the structural golden template and conform to Fura Online Judge importer logic (`D:\Workspaces\Github\furavietnam\furaoj`, strictly READONLY). Default import limits & score: 1 GB RAM (`<memory-limit>1073741824</memory-limit>`), 1s time limit (`<time-limit>1000</time-limit>`), and 1đ problem score. Default language directories are `english` and `vietnamese`. Mirror `problem.xml`, `tests/`, `statements/`, `statement-sections/`, `files/`, `solutions/`, `stresses/`, `scripts/`, root scripts, `tags`, and checker/validator resource relationships as applicable.

Include the actual `files/testlib.h` used by the package when testlib is used. Testlib C++ sources must use `#include <testlib.h>`.

Do not invent or guess unsupported Polygon XML. Build a clean staging directory and verify all descriptor paths against actual files before ZIP creation.


## Themis Package Standard

The companion Themis package ZIP must strictly conform to:
```text
<problemname>/
  TEST01/
    <problemname>.<ext_inp>
    <problemname>.<ext_out>
  TEST02/
    <problemname>.<ext_inp>
    <problemname>.<ext_out>
  ...
  TEST[NN]/
    <problemname>.<ext_inp>
    <problemname>.<ext_out>
```
- `<problemname>`: problem code / short name.
- `TEST[ID]`: folder name (`TEST01`..`TESTNN` matching %02d or %03d).
- `<problemname>.<ext_inp>` & `<problemname>.<ext_out>`: exact filenames and extensions specified in problem statement (or `<problemname>.INP` / `<problemname>.OUT` for standard I/O).
- All files must be byte-for-byte identical to Polygon tests and follow strict whitespace rules (zero trailing spaces, zero redundant empty lines, exact 1 newline at EOF).

After building both staging trees and final ZIPs, run the offline-package-verifier in offline mode against both packages. ZIP readability alone is insufficient.
